[ti:The Irish Rover]
[ar:Traditional]
[00:00.00]In the year of our Lord eighteen hundred and six
[00:11.36]We set sail from the coal quay of Cork
[00:19.12]We were sailing away with a cargo of bricks
[00:26.84]For the grand city hall in New York
[00:37.60]We'd an elegant craft, she was rigged fore and aft
[00:41.48]And oh, how the trade winds drove her
[00:45.30]She had twenty-three masts and she stood several blasts
[00:53.08]And they called her the Irish Rover
